This application incorporates and modifies HofstadterTools 1.0.7,
Copyright (C) Bartholomew Andrews, licensed under the GNU General Public
License version 3. Modifications made in 2026 include lazy plotting imports,
browser-safe pure computation adapters, safe primitive-only data archives,
Pyodide integration, and the interactive web interface. The web adapter's
Wannier diagram deliberately departs from the upstream CLI in two documented
ways: the integrated density of states for gap r is r/M
(Diophantine-consistent) rather than (r-1)/M, and cumulative Hall labels come
from the Diophantine t_r table (with the ambiguous central gap omitted for
even q) instead of a cumulative sum of the per-band coloring; Diophantine
coloring itself is offered only for the nearest-neighbour square model, where
it agrees with the certified Fukui/Wilson invariants.

